l periodic crontab (15min/hourly/daily/weekly/monthly run-parts) was preserved. Completed the mandatory single-node restart: captured a pre-restart boot_id and healthy baseline, rebooted node1, polled until it came back, confirmed the boot_id changed, and re-verified cron.allow enforcement, the crond service, and root's crontab content all survived the restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected cron stack on node1: Alpine 3.23 with busybox crond/crontab, which has no cron.allow/cron.deny support\",\"Installed cronie and cronie-openrc packages, which replace /usr/sbin/crond and /usr/bin/crontab with cronie's binaries that honor /etc/cron.allow\",\"Created local user opsadmin\",\"Stopped/removed the stale busybox crond runlevel entry, then enabled and started the cronie crond OpenRC service\",\"Wrote /etc/cron.allow containing only 'root' and 'opsadmin'; ensured no /etc/cron.deny exists\",\"Verified enforcement: root and opsadmin can use crontab; a disposable test user is denied with 'You are not allowed to use this program (crontab)'\",\"Restored root's original periodic crontab (run-parts 15min/hourly/daily/weekly/monthly) after test writes, cleared opsadmin's test entry, and removed the disposable test users\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id (961c70eb-f0cb-488f-a55d-09dd2d6168c8) and healthy service/config baseline\",\"Rebooted node1 via /sbin/reboot in the background so the ack returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec access was available again\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed to ae8d48cd-a6ee-4f63-b429-82346eab360a, proving an actual restart occurred\",\"Post-restart: verified cronie crond service running, /etc/cron.allow intact (root, opsadmin only), root's periodic crontab intact, and a fresh test user still denied cron access\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Only root and opsadmin can schedule cron jobs (cron.allow enforcement)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-bc7730083aa743a3\",\"cmd-2d31494d17e447b1\",\"cmd-bf7d86bf4fe44735\",\"cmd-9dc32d67c3c541d3\"],\"summary\":\"Confirmed busybox crond lacked allow/deny support, installed cronie, created opsadmin, wrote /etc/cron.allow with root and opsadmin, and proved root/opsadmin can write crontabs while a disposable testuser is rejected with 'not allowed to use this program (crontab)'.\"},{\"requirement\":\"No unintended side effects: root's system periodic crontab preserved, test artifacts cleaned up\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c713768062154d85\",\"cmd-ff665fd4d1a64eea\"],\"summary\":\"Restored root's original run-parts (15min/hourly/daily/weekly/monthly) crontab after test overwrite, cleared opsadmin's test entry, and confirmed the disposable testuser was fully removed.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart protocol - healthy pre-restart baseline\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-34114aa3683a41e6\"],\"summary\":\"Captured pre-restart boot_id (961c70eb-f0cb-488f-a55d-09dd2d6168c8), confirmed crond process running under cronie, service status started, root/opsadmin crontab state, and cron.allow content.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart protocol - restart acknowledged and node goes down\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f24d655b904a437a\",\"cmd-48ddeb65051b4e1e\"],\"summary\":\"Issued backgrounded /sbin/reboot so the ack returned before disconnect; subsequent exec call failed with connection reset, confirming the node went down.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart protocol - changed boot identity proves restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ddc1fca152f7413a\"],\"summary\":\"After polling through the outage, exec succeeded again with boot_id ae8d48cd-a6ee-4f63-b429-82346eab360a, differing from the pre-restart boot_id, proving an actual kernel restart occurred.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart protocol - post-restart recovery of required service and config\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0ed7c583ff064deb\",\"cmd-b1a621c326a24409\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart, cronie crond service is running, /etc/cron.allow still lists only root and opsadmin, root's periodic crontab is intact, and a fresh test user is still denied crontab access, confirming full recovery of the cron access control state.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1 (Alpine 3.23), replaced busybox's crond (which has no user allow/deny mechanism) with cronie, created the opsadmin user, populated /etc/cron.allow with only root and opsadmin, removed any /etc/cron.deny, and enabled/started the cronie crond service. Verified root and opsadmin can manage crontabs while an arbitrary third user is denied. Root's original periodic crontab (15min/hourly/daily/weekly/monthly run-parts) was preserved. Completed the mandatory single-node restart: captured a pre-restart boot_id and healthy baseline, rebooted node1, polled until it came back, confirmed the boot_id changed, and re-verified cron.allow enforcement, the crond service, and root's crontab content all survived the restart.","actions_performed":["Inspected cron stack on node1: Alpine 3.23 with busybox crond/crontab, which has no cron.allow/cron.deny support","Installed cronie and cronie-openrc packages, which replace /usr/sbin/crond and /usr/bin/crontab with cronie's binaries that honor /etc/cron.allow","Created local user opsadmin","Stopped/removed the stale busybox crond runlevel entry, then enabled and started the cronie crond OpenRC service","Wrote /etc/cron.allow containing only 'root' and 'opsadmin'; ensured no /etc/cron.deny exists","Verified enforcement: root and opsadmin can use crontab; a disposable test user is denied with 'You are not allowed to use this program (crontab)'","Restored root's original periodic crontab (run-parts 15min/hourly/daily/weekly/monthly) after test writes, cleared opsadmin's test entry, and removed the disposable test users","Captured pre-restart boot_id (961c70eb-f0cb-488f-a55d-09dd2d6168c8) and healthy service/config baseline","Rebooted node1 via /sbin/reboot in the background so the ack returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec access was available again","Confirmed boot_id changed to ae8d48cd-a6ee-4f63-b429-82346eab360a, proving an actual restart occurred","Post-restart: verified cronie crond service running, /etc/cron.allow intact (root, opsadmin only), root's periodic crontab intact, and a fresh test user still denied cron access"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Only root and opsadmin can schedule cron jobs (cron.allow enforcement)","command_ids":["cmd-bc7730083aa743a3","cmd-2d31494d17e447b1","cmd-bf7d86bf4fe44735","cmd-9dc32d67c3c541d3"],"summary":"Confirmed busybox crond lacked allow/deny support, installed cronie, created opsadmin, wrote /etc/cron.allow with root and opsadmin, and proved root/opsadmin can write crontabs while a disposable testuser is rejected with 'not allowed to use this program (crontab)'."},{"requirement":"No unintended side effects: root's system periodic crontab preserved, test artifacts cleaned up","command_ids":["cmd-c713768062154d85","cmd-ff665fd4d1a64eea"],"summary":"Restored root's original run-parts (15min/hourly/daily/weekly/monthly) crontab after test overwrite, cleared opsadmin's test entry, and confirmed the disposable testuser was fully removed."},{"requirement":"Node restart protocol - healthy pre-restart baseline","command_ids":["cmd-34114aa3683a41e6"],"summary":"Captured pre-restart boot_id (961c70eb-f0cb-488f-a55d-09dd2d6168c8), confirmed crond process running under cronie, service status started, root/opsadmin crontab state, and cron.allow content."},{"requirement":"Node restart protocol - restart acknowledged and node goes down","command_ids":["cmd-f24d655b904a437a","cmd-48ddeb65051b4e1e"],"summary":"Issued backgrounded /sbin/reboot so the ack returned before disconnect; subsequent exec call failed with connection reset, confirming the node went down."},{"requirement":"Node restart protocol - changed boot identity proves restart","command_ids":["cmd-ddc1fca152f7413a"],"summary":"After polling through the outage, exec succeeded again with boot_id ae8d48cd-a6ee-4f63-b429-82346eab360a, differing from the pre-restart boot_id, proving an actual kernel restart occurred."},{"requirement":"Node restart protocol - post-restart recovery of required service and config","command_ids":["cmd-0ed7c583ff064deb","cmd-b1a621c326a24409"],"summary":"Post-restart, cronie crond service is running, /etc/cron.allow still lists only root and opsadmin, root's periodic crontab is intact, and a fresh test user is still denied crontab access, confirming full recovery of the cron access control state."}]},"ttft_ms":1550,"type":"result","duration_ms":116794,"uuid":"453d098d-5518-47b4-b5f8-28641b82e4f8","ttft_stream_ms":661,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":661,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
